{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Make yourself an ark.</b> Rashi: 'much spirit,' etc. — until 'to bring a flood — perhaps they will repent.' All was revealed before Him that they would not repent, but corresponding to the attribute of mercy, which sought mercy for them — Rashi, thus. And so you may also explain regarding ויהי הגשם: it was revealed before Him that they would not repent, but to quiet from upon Him the attribute of mercy that had been advocating merits for them, He brought down the waters gently before it, and it saw that they did not repent." "<b>Wood of gofer.</b> Sulfur comes forth from it, and it does not dissolve in water. And He commanded to take this wood to show them with what they are fit to be judged." "<b>And you shall pitch it within and without with pitch.</b> Our Rabbis, of blessed memory, said: they sinned with boiling waters, and with boiling waters they were judged. And if you ask: how could the pitch hold — was it not dissolved in the boiling waters? One may answer: it was a miracle within a miracle. And another interpretation: the waters around the ark were cool, for if you do not say so, how did Sihon and Og his brother escape — according to the one who says the flood descended upon the land of Israel?"], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "The opening words 'הרבה רוח וכו׳' and 'פרש״‎י כך' are mechanical citations of Rashi's comment on this verse; the abbreviation וכו׳ is rendered 'etc.'", 2 "Reading 'זפת' (pitch) in the question, consistent with the verse's 'כפר' (pitch/bitumen) and the context of waterproofing."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:03:18.099703768Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}